","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"milestoned","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2018-05-07T16:25:17Z","milestone":{"title":"GLM 0.9.9"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/issues/comments/395871401","html_url":"https://github.com/g-truc/glm/issues/723#issuecomment-395871401","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/issues/723","id":395871401,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5NTg3MTQwMQ==","user":{"login":"himikof","id":43698,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNjk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43698?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/himikof","html_url":"https://github.com/himikof","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/himikof/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/himikof/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/himikof/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/himikof/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/himikof/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/himikof/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/himikof/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/himikof/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/himikof/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-06-08T19:52:49Z","updated_at":"2018-06-08T19:52:49Z","body":"The code added in 384dab0 is actually explicitly checking for IEEE 754 floating point types and using `std::memcmp` for them, and continues to use `==` operator otherwise. The commit is about silencing compiler warnings, but I fail to see any possible warnings that could be suppressed in this way.\r\nIf this is perhaps an optimization, then it is strange that the new equality comparison functions are still called member-wise in a loop, which is much inferior to calling `std::memcpy` on a continuous memory range once.\r\n\r\nBut this is still a silent/unexpected breaking change not mentioned in 0.9.9 release notes, so this bug being labeled an enhancement is strange. I think that this part of the change should be either reverted, or provided with an explicit opt-out and some documentation/explanation.\r\n\r\nI personally think that comparing IEEE 754 types not by IEEE 754 rules is very unexpected and does not actually match glsl semantics. And modern hardware often has direct support for efficient IEEE 754 comparisons.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/issues/comments/395871401/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"himikof","id":43698,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNjk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43698?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/himikof","html_url":"https://github.com/himikof","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/himikof/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/himikof/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/himikof/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/himikof/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/himikof/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/himikof/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github